# STIG RHEL-09-653120: RHEL 9 must allocate an audit_backlog_limit of sufficient size to capture proces
# STIG ID: V-258173 (LOW)

META
    esp_id `r9-rhel-09-653120-grub-audit-param-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `rocky9`
    criticality `medium`

    title `STIG RHEL-09-653120: RHEL 9 must allocate an audit_backlog_limit of sufficient size to capture proces`
    description `RHEL 9 must allocate an audit_backlog_limit of sufficient size to capture processes that start prior to the audit daemon.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `rhel9,stig,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:RHEL-09-653120,NIST-800-53:AU-14(1),NIST-800-53:AU-4`
    control_objective `AU-14(1)`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Rocky9:localhost:os-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `90`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for RHEL-09-653120.`

    component_id `comp-r9-os`

    impl_AU_14_1 `This control is validated by checking /etc/default/grub for the required configuration.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target_file
        path `/etc/default/grub`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE content_check
        content string contains `audit=1`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN file_content
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF content_check
            OBJECT_REF target_file
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
